   "search_text": "6   A student attempts to solve the equation\n\n                                 cos x + sin x tan x = 2 sin x −1\n\n       in the range 0 ≤x ≤2π.\n\n     The student’s attempt is as follows:\n\n\n           cos x + sin x tan x = 2 sin x −1\n\n\n\n         So   cos x −sin x + sin x tan x −sin x = −1                             (I)\n\n\n\n         So   (sin x −cos x)(tan x −1) = −1                                     (II)\n\n\n\n         So   sin x −cos x = −1  or tan x −1 = −1                             (III)\n\n\n         So   (sin x −cos x)2 = 1  or tan x = 0                            (IV)\n\n\n\n         So  2 sin x cos x = 0  or tan x = 0                             (V)\n\n\n         So  x = 0, π2, π, 3π2 , 2π                                         (VI)\n\n\n\n     Which of the following best describes this attempt?\n\n\n   A  It is completely correct\n\n   B  It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (I)\n\n   C  It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (II)\n\n   D  It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error occurs on line (III)\n\n    E   It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is that extra solutions were introduced on\n           line (IV)\n\n    F   It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is that extra solutions were introduced on\n           line (V)\n\n   G  It is incorrect, and the ﬁrst error is not eliminating the values where tan x is\n        undeﬁned on line (VI)\n",
